      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"snapshotId\":\"capture-630c1226-628b-4cfb-9aa8-02074d2f0ff6\",\"url\":\"https://docs.python.org/3.12/whatsnew/3.12.html\",\"title\":\"What’s New In Python 3.12 — Python 3.12.15 documentation\",\"capturedAt\":\"2026-10-10T03:09:50.935Z\",\"text\":\"[characters 1608-1645]\\nPEP 684, a unique per-interpreter GIL\\n\\n[characters 9840-9870]\\nPEP 684: A Per-Interpreter GIL\\n\\n[characters 9872-10163]\\nPEP 684 introduces a per-interpreter GIL, so that sub-interpreters may now be created with a unique GIL per interpreter. This allows Python programs to take full advantage of multiple CPU cores. This is currently only available through the C-API, though a Python API is anticipated for 3.13.\\n\\n[characters 10165-10258]\\nUse the new Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig() function to create an interpreter with its own GIL:\\n\\n[characters 10260-10582]\\nPyInterpreterConfig config = {\\n    .check_multi_interp_extensions = 1,\\n    .gil = PyInterpreterConfig_OWN_GIL,\\n};\\nPyThreadState *tstate = NULL;\\nPyStatus status = Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig(&tstate, &config);\\nif (PyStatus_Exception(status)) {\\n    return -1;\\n}\\n/* The new interpreter is now active in the current thread. */\\n\\n[characters 10585-10715]\\nFor further examples how to use the C-API for sub-interpreters with a per-interpreter GIL, see Modules/_xxsubinterpretersmodule.c.\\n\\n[characters 78539-78658]\\nPEP 683: Introduce Immortal Objects, which allows objects to bypass reference counts, and related changes to the C-API:\\n\\n[characters 79359-79602]\\nPEP 684: Add the new Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig() function and PyInterpreterConfig, which may be used to create sub-interpreters with their own GILs. (See PEP 684: A Per-Interpreter GIL for more info.) (Contributed by Eric Snow in gh-104110.)\\n\\n[characters 80131-80482]\\ntp_weaklist for all static builtin types is always NULL. This is an internal-only field on PyTypeObject but we’re pointing out the change in case someone happens to be accessing the field directly anyway. To avoid breakage, consider using the existing public C-API instead, or, if necessary, the (internal-only) _PyObject_GET_WEAKREFS_LISTPTR() macro.\",\"truncated\":true,\"query\":\"per-interpreter GIL sub-interpreters C-API Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig\",\"excerpts\":[{\"charStart\":1608,\"charEnd\":1645,\"text\":\"PEP 684, a unique per-interpreter GIL\"},{\"charStart\":9840,\"charEnd\":9870,\"text\":\"PEP 684: A Per-Interpreter GIL\"},{\"charStart\":9872,\"charEnd\":10163,\"text\":\"PEP 684 introduces a per-interpreter GIL, so that sub-interpreters may now be created with a unique GIL per interpreter. This allows Python programs to take full advantage of multiple CPU cores. This is currently only available through the C-API, though a Python API is anticipated for 3.13.\"},{\"charStart\":10165,\"charEnd\":10258,\"text\":\"Use the new Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig() function to create an interpreter with its own GIL:\"},{\"charStart\":10260,\"charEnd\":10582,\"text\":\"PyInterpreterConfig config = {\\n    .check_multi_interp_extensions = 1,\\n    .gil = PyInterpreterConfig_OWN_GIL,\\n};\\nPyThreadState *tstate = NULL;\\nPyStatus status = Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig(&tstate, &config);\\nif (PyStatus_Exception(status)) {\\n    return -1;\\n}\\n/* The new interpreter is now active in the current thread. */\"},{\"charStart\":10585,\"charEnd\":10715,\"text\":\"For further examples how to use the C-API for sub-interpreters with a per-interpreter GIL, see Modules/_xxsubinterpretersmodule.c.\"},{\"charStart\":78539,\"charEnd\":78658,\"text\":\"PEP 683: Introduce Immortal Objects, which allows objects to bypass reference counts, and related changes to the C-API:\"},{\"charStart\":79359,\"charEnd\":79602,\"text\":\"PEP 684: Add the new Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig() function and PyInterpreterConfig, which may be used to create sub-interpreters with their own GILs. (See PEP 684: A Per-Interpreter GIL for more info.) (Contributed by Eric Snow in gh-104110.)\"},{\"charStart\":80131,\"charEnd\":80482,\"text\":\"tp_weaklist for all static builtin types is always NULL. This is an internal-only field on PyTypeObject but we’re pointing out the change in case someone happens to be accessing the field directly anyway. To avoid breakage, consider using the existing public C-API instead, or, if necessary, the (internal-only) _PyObject_GET_WEAKREFS_LISTPTR() macro.\"}],\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\Temp\\\\weftmate-fact1-32453ca3-ce97-4ece-8ea1-120b2180dc3f\\\\profile\\\\conversations\\\\be02ee38d3982f0d63a1fde99286ad6e6c6bb84f1674ceced8222269cc953289\\\\session-5469ded3-3257-4b59-af66-58ddf89ff324\\\\.weftmate-web-sources\\\\capture-630c1226-628b-4cfb-9aa8-02074d2f0ff6.txt\"}"
